# Filter drivers for this repository.
#
# The driver itself is defined in .git/config, which git does not clone, so a
# fresh checkout sees this line, finds no `automode` filter, and passes the
# content through untouched. That is a safe default -- the file arrives stripped,
# which is what an unconfigured machine should get -- but it is also silent, so
# the two `git config` commands are a named bootstrap step in README.
#
# .gitfilters/automode-clean strips `autoMode` on the way into the index and
# .gitfilters/automode-smudge restores it on the way out. Both carry their own
# explanation of why the key cannot live in .claude/settings.local.json instead.
/.claude/settings.json filter=automode
